.TH PRAYER 1 "September 2026" "prayer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prayer \- calculate daily Islamic prayer times using libmuslim
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prayer
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print today's Fajr, sunrise, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha for a configured
location. With no arguments, use the configuration's default location.
Missing location information is an error. The default method is MWL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--location " city
Exact city name in the offline configuration, or a label with --coordinates.
.TP
.BI "--config " file
Use a specific locations JSON file.
.TP
.B --auto
Call geome --json once to obtain approximate IP-based city and coordinates.
Geome 1.0 has neither city lookup nor timezone output. If absent, the system
timezone is used with a warning. Use --timezone to override it.
.TP
.BI "--coordinates " latitude,longitude
Use coordinates directly, without geome or configuration.
.TP
.BI "--timezone " zone
Override the timezone with an IANA name in /usr/share/zoneinfo.
.TP
.BI "--method " id
Select mwl, isna, ummalqura, egypt, karachi, kemenag, gulf, or moonsighting.
Other named upstream methods are accepted. Custom/unknown methods fail.
.TP
.B --next
Print the next prayer's name, date and time. Sunrise is not a next prayer.
.TP
.B --current
Print the current prayer window, or None. Mutually exclusive with --next.
.TP
.B --hijri
Add today's civil tabular Hijri date to human output.
.TP
.B --json
Print the full JSON schedule, including both dates, method, location,
prayer_dates, next and current. Unavailable values are null.
.TP
.BI "--at " seconds
Use this integer Unix timestamp instead of the current system time.
.TP
.B --help
Print help without network access.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/prayer/locations.json or, if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or
relative, $HOME/.config/prayer/locations.json. The JSON object contains a
default city name and a locations object keyed by city name. Each entry
requires numeric latitude and longitude and a timezone string. Files are
limited to 64 KiB and are never written by the program. See README for examples.
.SH CONVENTIONS
Dates from 1600 through 2200 CE are accepted. Independent upstream ephemeris
validation covers 1900 through 2100. Times are estimates and round upward
to whole minutes. Timezone offsets are applied at each event, including DST.
Dates outside the schedule day are retained in output.
.PP
Fajr ends at sunrise. There is no active obligatory-prayer window between
sunrise and Dhuhr. Other windows end at the next prayer; Isha ends at next
Fajr for scheduling purposes, not as a religious ruling on preferred times.
Missing boundaries yield no active window.
.PP
High-latitude prayer estimates follow upstream's method policies. Sunrise
is never substituted and can be unavailable. The Makkah Isha interval is
the upstream fixed interval; this application adds no Ramadan adjustment.
Tabular Hijri dates change at civil midnight, not sunset, and can differ
from official or sighting-based calendars.
.SH PRIVACY
Only --auto uses the network. Geome sends an HTTPS request to ipwho.is,
which receives the public IP. VPNs and proxies can alter the apparent city.
No location is stored. Invocation is shell-free, capped at 15 seconds and
64 KiB of output. Offline configurations and help do not access the network.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: success. 2: invalid options. 3: configuration, dependency, data or I/O failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
prayer --coordinates 32.7765,-79.9311 --timezone America/New_York
prayer --location 'Charleston, US' --next
prayer --auto --timezone America/New_York --json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hijri (1),
.BR geome (1)